        "answer": "No. GitHub’s Active Malware or Exploits policy expressly allows dual-use content and supports posting content used for research into vulnerabilities, malware, or exploits, citing its educational value and net benefit to the security community [S1]. It states that restrictions are not intended to purge or restrict dual-use content in perpetuity, and that any restrictions in rare widespread-abuse cases are temporary where feasible [S1].\n\nThat said, the policy does allow restrictions in rare cases of very widespread abuse of dual-use content, potentially including disabling access or full removal as a last resort, to disrupt an ongoing unlawful attack or malware campaign [S1]. So removal is not automatic based on potential misuse; it is tied to actual abuse and is generally temporary [S1].",
